# ── LaTeX source (vendored) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# paper/ is ALSO its own git repo, cloned from Overleaf
# (git.overleaf.com/69c12469b917d4e261cb82c3). The .tex and the figures
# it references are tracked here too, so that sessions without access
# to this machine -- or to the Overleaf credentials -- can still read
# and edit the paper.
#
# Consequence to keep in mind: between syncs there are two copies. This
# repo is the working copy; Overleaf is updated by pushing from INSIDE
# paper/ (it has its own origin) when you're next at the Mac. Avoid
# editing both in the same stretch of work, or you'll be reconciling by
# hand.
#
# Note `paper/*` rather than `paper/` -- git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so the directory itself has to
# stay visible and its contents excluded piecewise for the negations
# below to take effect.
paper/*
!paper/*.tex
!paper/*.png
!paper/*.bib

# ── Python ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Generated plots -- reproducible by rerunning verification_tests.py /
# publication_plots.py, so not worth versioning binary PNGs that change
# on every run. Remove this line if you'd rather pin the exact figures
# that went into a given draft.
figures/

# ── Fortran / CMake build artefacts (Training_code/) ─────────────────
build/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
Makefile.cmake
*.o
*.mod
*.smod
*.a
*.so
a.out
gmon.out
*.bin

# The bare `out` binaries produced by the 1D/2D diffusion makefiles.
# Anchored per-directory rather than a bare `out` so a future source
# file or folder legitimately named "out.f90"/"out/" elsewhere isn't
# silently swallowed.
Training_code/1D_Diffusion/out
Training_code/2D_Diffusion/out

# ── macOS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
